Generate the autocompletion script for chab for the specified shell.
See each sub-command's help for details on how to use the generated script.

Usage:
  chab completion [flags]
  chab completion [command]

Available Commands:
  bash        Generate the autocompletion script for bash
  fish        Generate the autocompletion script for fish
  powershell  Generate the autocompletion script for powershell
  zsh         Generate the autocompletion script for zsh

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for completion

Global Flags:
      --api-base-url string   API base URL (Chab default uses www.chab.ai/v1; custom base URLs use <base-url>/v1)
      --auth-file string      path to the CLI auth file
      --base-url string       product web base URL
      --config string         path to the CLI config file
      --debug                 write redacted request details to stderr
      --include-meta          include safe response metadata in machine output where supported
      --jq string             filter supported JSON output with a jq expression
      --json                  print stable JSON output where supported
      --locale string         response language sent as Accept-Language (en or de)
      --no-ansi               disable ANSI terminal controls and paging where supported
      --no-color              disable color in human output where supported
      --no-pager              disable pager use for long human output where supported
      --no-prompt             fail instead of prompting for interactive input
      --plain                 print copy-safe plain output where supported
      --profile string        profile to use for this invocation
      --template string       render supported JSON output with a Go text/template
      --yes                   accept supported confirmations for risky or destructive operations; does not supply missing input

Use "chab completion [command] --help" for more information about a command.
